From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NCM's packet signature follows the computer's choices, as in
 later kernels: set when the function resets, and worked out again after every
 request, so it matches the packet format (16- or 32-bit) as well as the CRC
 mode. It was set only by the CRC mode request, for the 16-bit format: macOS
 and Linux keep that format, Windows doesn't, so on Windows the Brick threw
 away every packet ("Wrong NDP SIGN") and sent its own with the wrong
 signature

---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
@@ -532,6 +532,7 @@
 {
 	ncm->parser_opts = &ndp16_opts;
 	ncm->is_crc = false;
+	ncm->ndp_sign = ncm->parser_opts->ndp_sign;
 	ncm->port.cdc_filter = DEFAULT_FILTER;
 
 	/* doesn't make sense for ncm, fixed size used */
@@ -846,6 +847,8 @@
 			ctrl->bRequestType, ctrl->bRequest,
 			w_value, w_index, w_length);
 	}
+	ncm->ndp_sign = ncm->parser_opts->ndp_sign |
+		(ncm->is_crc ? NCM_NDP_HDR_CRC : 0);
 
 	/* respond with data transfer or status phase? */
 	if (value >= 0) {
